General store:
{{External|rs=General stores|rsc=General Store}}
The '''general store''' is a type of shop placed in many locations in ''[[RuneScape]]''. Unlike [[specialty shop]]s, general stores usually accept all tradeable items, making them a useful place to sell miscellaneous goods that do not have a dedicated store. General stores are identified on the [[map]] by a pot [[File:General store icon.png]] [[icon]]. Many general stores have both a [[shop keeper]] and a [[shop assistant]], both of which can be used to access the shop stock.

==Staples==
[[File:Lumbridge General Store.png|thumb|250px|A typical general store.]]
Each general store carries a few commonly used, inexpensive items. It rarely runs out of these items for long, as they tend to restock quickly. The following is the most conventional inventory for a general store:
*[[Pot]]
*[[Jug]]
*[[Empty jug pack]]
*[[Shears]]
*[[Bucket]]
*[[Bowl]]
*[[Cake tin]]
*[[Tinderbox]]
*[[Chisel]]
*[[Hammer]]
Most general stores available in the [[free-to-play]] map area also carry the following:
*[[Newcomer map]]
*[[Security book]]
Other common items for the general store include:
*[[Rope]]
*[[Knife]]
*[[Vial of water]]
*[[Pestle and mortar]]
*[[Candle]]
*[[Unlit torch]]
*[[Cooked meat]]
*[[Bronze pickaxe]]
*[[Bronze axe]]
*[[Iron axe]]
*[[Spade]]

==Anything goes==
[[File:Lumbridge General Store stock.png|thumb|The stock of a typical general store.]]
In addition to regular stock, players may sell any tradeable item to a store, so the general store in each town will often have a stock of the local specialty, though any item can be sold to any location. A player can buy any item in the general store that they want if they have enough money. Bargains may sometimes be found from players unaware of typically higher street prices, or in too much of a hurry to find a buyer.

===Player sell prices===
When selling to a general store, the price when it has no stock of that item is the low alchemy value, i.e. 40% of the item's in-game [[value]] (the item's stock price when buying from a [[specialty shop]]). The minimum price the player receives for selling any item is 10% of the item's [[value]], so 25% of the item's initial (low alchemy/general store) price.

Every overstocked item causes the selling price to decrease by a certain percentage of the item's value. Since all [[Free-to-play|free to play]] stores have this value at 3%, this causes the minimum price (10% of the item's [[value]]) to be reached after the store is overstocked with 10 of that item, the lowest value is 0.3% reaching the minimum after 100 items.

<math>\text{Sell price} = \text{Value}  \times \frac{\text{Max}(10,  \text{BuyPercentage} - \text{Stock} \times \text{ChangePercentage} )}{100}</math>

For example, [[tiara]] has a [[value]] of 100 [[coins]] and a Low Alch price of 40 coins so the first tiara is sold for that. The lowest price that tiaras go for is 10% of item's [[value]] which is 10 coins. Each sold tiara decreases the price by 3% of 100 coins = 3 coins.

<math>\text{Sell price} = 100  \times \frac{\text{Max}(10,  \text{40} - \text{Stock} \times \text{3} )}{100} = \text{Max}(10,  \text{40} - \text{Stock} \times \text{3} )</math>

'''Note:''' The general stores in the [[Bandit Camp (Wilderness)|Wilderness Bandit Camp]] ([[Bandit Duty Free|Bandit Duty Free General Store]]), and in [[Rogues' Den]] ([[Martin Thwait's Lost and Found]]) will buy items at a high alchemy price, which is 60% of its [[value]], or 150% of the price offered in normal general stores. The general stores in [[West Ardougne]] ([[West Ardougne General Store]]), [[Pollnivneach]] ([[Pollnivneach general store.|Pollnivneach general store]]), and the [[Legends' Guild]] ([[Legends Guild General Store.|Legends Guild General Store]]) will buy items at 55% of their [[value]], or 137.5% of the price offered in normal general stores.

'''Note for members:''' Given the combinations: the [[Martin Thwait's Lost and Found]] is the best place to sell items up to 10 at a time,  up to 44 items the 55%-1% stores give the best value (for example the [[Legends Guild General Store.|Legends Guild General Store]]). If selling more items at once the [[Void Knight General Store]] and [[Jennifer's General Supplies]] offer the best prices given the low change value. If selling tiara's (with the value of 100), selling 10 gives {{Coins|550}}, {{Coins|550}} and {{Coins|423}} and 100 gives {{Coins|1660}}, {{Coins|2045}} and {{Coins|2525}} respectively.

===Player buy prices===
When buying items from a general store, the price starts at 127% of the item's [[value]] with 1 item in stock and decreases by 3% (in F2P) with each extra item stocked until it reaches 30% of the item's [[value]] at 34 items in stock.

<math>\text{Buy price} = \text{Max}\left(\frac{\text{Value} \times (130 - 3 \times \text{Stock})}{100}, \frac{30 \times \text{Value}}{100}\right)</math>

