A '''sawmill''' is a [[shop]] which also serves as a facility, and facilitates the creation of planks. The [[sawmill operator]] working there can turn seven different kinds of [[logs]] into [[planks]] for a fee, and also sells [[Construction]] supplies: [[saw]]s, [[bolt of cloth|bolts of cloth]], and three kinds of [[nails]]; they share the same stock. Players can have their logs converted to planks by using the sawmill operator's "''Buy planks''" option. He is able to create regular [[plank]]s, [[oak plank]]s, [[teak plank]]s, [[mahogany plank]]s, [[camphor plank]]s, [[ironwood plank]]s, and [[rosewood plank]]s for the player assuming they have the requisite '''unnoted''' logs and enough [[coins]].

There are currently four sawmills that are known to exist in [[Gielinor]]. One sawmill is in the [[Lumber Yard]] north-east of [[Varrock]], another is in the [[Woodcutting Guild]], a third in [[Prifddinas]], and a fourth in [[Auburnvale]]. Access to the sawmill in the Woodcutting Guild requires 60 [[Woodcutting]] in order to enter the Woodcutting Guild. The sawmill in Prifddinas requires completion of [[Song of the Elves]]. The sawmill in [[Auburnvale]] is less than half the distance to a bank than the one in the Woodcutting Guild, making it the closest sawmill to a bank of all sawmill locations.

[[Sawmill voucher|Sawmill vouchers]] can be redeemed at any sawmill to receive twice as many planks per log. For example, a player that converts 1 [[Rosewood logs|Rosewood log]] with 1 sawmill voucher in their inventory will receive 2 [[Rosewood plank|Rosewood planks]], saving {{Coins|7500}} and the time that would have been spent woodcutting.
[[File:Sawmill interface.png|thumb|The interface to convert logs into planks.]]

